# inc-jwm0. A character in heavy armour must be able to tear out of glue on
# his Strength, because he can never pass the Escape Artist check.
#
# THE SUBJECT is the human paladin of chargen-paladin.keys, and he is chosen
# because he is the WORST case rather than a convenient one: seed 4 rolls him
# STR 10, so his Strength check is a flat d20 with no bonus at all. A real
# tank rolls better. If this character gets out, every heavier-armed, stronger
# one does.
#
# THE GEAR is full plate armour, taken in wizard mode, plus the kite shield he
# starts with, readied. That is Escape Artist -11: 0 ranks, +1 DEX (full plate
# caps the bonus at +1), -12 armour. The escape DC is 14 -- 15 + the STUCK
# magnitude, which is -1 for every hazard in the game because nothing ever
# sets one (inc-18q6). His Escape Artist ceiling is therefore 20 - 11 = 9,
# five below the floor, and no roll can close it.
#
# THE HAZARD is "tanglefoot strands", written under the two squares east of
# him with the wizard terrain command. It is [j] on page 2 of that menu, hence
# the TAB. Walking in costs a flat Reflex DC 15 (lib/alchemy.irh:282), which
# he fails at -1.
#
# THE ORACLE is the two printed check lines. "Strength Check:" cannot appear
# on a tree without the fix -- that is the assertion that discriminates. The
# escape itself is NOT enough on its own, because Skills.cpp:1600 already
# frees him on a natural 20 while no hostile is within sixteen squares, and
# this fixture deliberately runs in an empty room. See tools/check_entangle_escape.sh.
#
# Twenty attempts. At STR 10 each attempt is 35%, so twenty of them fail
# together about one time in ten thousand -- and the seed is fixed, so it
# either passes or it does not.

@include chargen-paladin.keys
@until "Afoot" ESC

w
@expect "Enter wizard mode"
y
e
@until ": Armours" RIGHT
@until "Full plate armour" DOWN
DOWN
ENTER
j
SPACE
d
ESC
i
f
SPACE
a
SPACE
ESC
d
@dump:geared
ESC

# already in wizard mode: 'w' opens the menu with no y/n
w
K
RIGHT
ENTER
TAB
j

RIGHT
@while "Confirm" y
@dump:entered
